WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.487 --> 00:00:02.825
- Usually people are really confused

00:00:02.825 --> 00:00:04.840
when I tell them what I do.

00:00:04.840 --> 00:00:08.761
I tell them, like, yeah, I
own a fingerboard company.

00:00:08.761 --> 00:00:10.945
Like those Tech Decks you
used to get in something.

00:00:10.945 --> 00:00:12.862
Yeah, but professional.

00:00:25.934 --> 00:00:29.184
Skateboarding makes me feel awesome.

00:00:29.184 --> 00:00:31.044
It doesn't get boring.

00:00:31.044 --> 00:00:33.073
It's always a challenge.

00:00:33.073 --> 00:00:35.161
There's no rules.

00:00:35.161 --> 00:00:39.161
Fingerboarding and
skateboarding both have that.

00:00:46.145 --> 00:00:48.425
I started fingerboarding in fourth grade.

00:00:48.425 --> 00:00:50.564
I had a lot of fun playing
with the Tech Decks

00:00:50.564 --> 00:00:54.464
and then I wanted to kind of improve them.

00:00:54.464 --> 00:00:56.756
A lot of times the screws would
come out so I'd glue them in

00:00:56.756 --> 00:00:59.558
and just start modifying things like that.

00:00:59.558 --> 00:01:03.348
And I just realized I could
make them better and better.

00:01:03.348 --> 00:01:04.493
A lot of kids wanted to buy them

00:01:04.493 --> 00:01:06.538
so I kinda put a name on it

00:01:06.538 --> 00:01:10.371
and it grew into this
huge business over time.

00:01:11.239 --> 00:01:13.596
There's hundreds of thousands of people

00:01:13.596 --> 00:01:16.013
out there that are into this.

00:01:19.449 --> 00:01:22.193
We are at the Flat Face
rendezvous location

00:01:22.193 --> 00:01:23.897
in Dracut, Massachusetts

00:01:23.897 --> 00:01:26.775
and it's pretty much a big building

00:01:26.775 --> 00:01:28.256
filled with fingerboard parks

00:01:28.256 --> 00:01:30.008
and I do huge events here

00:01:30.008 --> 00:01:32.484
where kids fly in from all over the place

00:01:32.484 --> 00:01:35.234
to come and fingerboard together.

00:01:36.858 --> 00:01:37.875
When you go into a contest,

00:01:37.875 --> 00:01:39.676
it's crazy cuz there's stadium seating

00:01:39.676 --> 00:01:40.889
and there's everyone looking at you

00:01:40.889 --> 00:01:43.074
and lighting and cameras.

00:01:43.074 --> 00:01:45.440
My first few contests, I
got a crazy adrenaline rush.

00:01:45.440 --> 00:01:46.396
Like, you don't even remember

00:01:46.396 --> 00:01:49.063
the thing after you do your run.

00:01:50.296 --> 00:01:52.243
I don't do any warm-ups or exercises

00:01:52.243 --> 00:01:54.155
with my hands for fingerboarding.

00:01:54.155 --> 00:01:57.405
Apparently some people do calisthenics.

00:01:58.754 --> 00:02:02.028
The rules are pretty much
you want to use two fingers.

00:02:02.028 --> 00:02:04.924
You'll have maybe 30
seconds or a minute or so

00:02:04.924 --> 00:02:06.138
and you just do a run

00:02:06.138 --> 00:02:08.701
and there'll be a whole bunch of judges.

00:02:08.701 --> 00:02:11.427
They'll judge you on consistency, style,

00:02:11.427 --> 00:02:15.594
the tricks you do and it's
like really high pressure.

00:02:19.562 --> 00:02:21.286
You can't even really put it into words.

00:02:21.286 --> 00:02:24.786
It's a crazy kinda feeling and atmosphere.

00:02:26.450 --> 00:02:29.297
When so many people get together
from all over the world,

00:02:29.297 --> 00:02:31.578
all over the country, and some of them,

00:02:31.578 --> 00:02:34.744
it's like a really,
really big deal to them.

00:02:34.744 --> 00:02:39.496
Like, that's the only thing
they want to do all year.

00:02:39.496 --> 00:02:42.915
It just makes me super happy
because I can barely believe

00:02:42.915 --> 00:02:45.555
that I'm the reason they're there.

00:02:45.555 --> 00:02:46.903
Like, because of something that I set up

00:02:46.903 --> 00:02:48.486
and that I'm doing.

